  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...One more round of some showers and thunderstorms \nlooks to affect the area late day today into this evening. \nIsolated to scattered severe thunderstorms will be possible with\nthis round mainly for our southernmost counties in Delmarva. \n\nHeading into the day today, a diffuse frontal boundary will \nremain near the area but it will be a bit farther south compared\nto Thursday. As a result, we do expect one more round of some \nshowers and thunderstorms to affect the area late afternoon into\nthe evening but the severe weather threat will be more limited \nin areal extent. In fact at this point only our southernmost \ncounties in Delmarva are highlighted by the Storm Prediction \nCenter as areas that could see isolated to scattered severe \nthunderstorms. Damaging winds look to be the biggest threat with\nany storms that turn severe. Also, heavy rainfall will be \npossible with any storms and this could lead to localized flash \nflooding if any training of storms were to develop. Otherwise it\nwill be another warm and humid day although not as much so as \nThursday. Heat indices look to top out in the 80s north and the \n90s south which is below Heat Advisory criteria. \n\nStorms may linger into this evening before moving out \novernight.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...The Labor Day Weekend will feature mostly dry \nweather with at or below normal temperatures and lower humidity.\n\nBy Saturday, the trend among model guidance shows the frontal \nboundary south of our region, with Canadian high pressure \nbuilding in across the Northeast and Mid-Atlantic. This will \nlargely end any shower and thunderstorm potential. Thus, Labor \nDay Weekend is still shaping up to feature nice weather, with \ntemperatures trending at or slightly below normal and lower \nhumidity.",
